From 548fed77195aa508b3d150f10c0d16fb72616e63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:20:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/52] Convert CreatePropHPR's rotation with FUN_004F0CB0, not
 MatrixToQuat

CreatePropHPR builds its heading/pitch/roll matrix with FUN_006D1E30
and converts it with FUN_004F0CB0 (0x006FC2E3: x = m21 - m12,
y = m02 - m20, z = m10 - m01), the same conversion CreateUnitHPR uses.
The recovery called func_MatrixToQuat (0x004EB3F0), which has the
opposite lane order, so every prop created through it -- all map props,
mass and hydrocarbon deposits -- got the conjugate orientation: its
heading mirrored, and its collision box turned the other way.

Found by replaying an FAF recording: the commander warp-in's
DamageRing hit a different set of trees than the shipped engine (the
ring test runs against the props' oriented collision boxes), and the
random stream diverged from there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d39d9ef11870dcb0a5070f48d165b8580219ff26)
(cherry picked from commit 3aa6e249caf66e386cca1b7c55a77f498f01c629)
---
 src/sdk/moho/entity/Prop.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sdk/moho/entity/Prop.cpp b/src/sdk/moho/entity/Prop.cpp
index ce8be57e..a1a8ec3e 100644
--- a/src/sdk/moho/entity/Prop.cpp
+++ b/src/sdk/moho/entity/Prop.cpp
@@ -390,7 +390,10 @@ namespace moho
     transform.pos_.x = posX;
     transform.pos_.y = posY;
     transform.pos_.z = posZ;
-    (void)MatrixToQuat(rotationMatrix, &transform.orient_);
+    // 0x006FC2E3 converts with FUN_004F0CB0 (x = m21 - m12, ...), as CreateUnitHPR does -- not with
+    // func_MatrixToQuat (0x004EB3F0), whose opposite lane order gave every map prop the conjugate
+    // orientation (a mirrored heading, and collision boxes turned the wrong way).
+    (void)MatrixRowsToQuatCanonical(rotationMatrix, &transform.orient_);
 
     Prop* const prop = PROP_Create(sim, transform, blueprintId.c_str());
     if (prop == nullptr) {
